  "interpretation": "n_subjects_straddling_partitions is the direct measurement: how many true patients have scans on both sides of a partition boundary. Under subject_only it should rise with the deletion fraction, because every scan whose identifier was removed becomes a free-floating singleton. Under component_safe it should rise more slowly, because session_id and series_uid edges do not take subject_id as an input and continue to bind scans that same_subject can no longer reach. The difference between the two curves is what the leakage-graph layer buys, measured rather than argued."
